    "show_share": true,
    "description": "A visit to the  Shimoni Slave Caves  in Kwale, Mombasa, is a reminder of the horror that human beings are capable of. Roughly hewn and averaging about 5-kilometres-long, the Shimoni caves were used as a holding area for slaves before they were ferried away. Even today, old iron shackles, wooden crates, rusted chains, and metal studs that were once used are still visible and preserved as a reminder of these atrocities.",
